failmalloc.c : LD_PRELOAD malloc fault injector used by the CLI-10, CLI-15, CLI-22 and PS2-G26-1 reproducers.
  gcc -O1 -fPIC -shared failmalloc.c -o failmalloc.so -ldl
  FAILMALLOC_AT=N          fail the N-th malloc/calloc/realloc call of the process
  FAILMALLOC_FUNC=sym      count only allocations whose immediate caller is the exported function "sym"
  FAILMALLOC_NTH=k         ... and fail the k-th of them (default 1)
  FAILMALLOC_TRACE=1       print what was failed and the counts at exit
Use it with a NON-sanitized build ($WORK/plain: the asan tree with -fsanitize removed from Makefile.inc),
since ASan's own allocator would be displaced by the preload. With mpirun, pass the variables with -x.
Internal libscotch symbols are renamed (_SCOTCHmemAllocGroup, _SCOTCHmeshGraphDual) under SCOTCH_RENAME.
